The cast from `const char*` to `char*` violates const-correctness. While `execve` family functions take `char**` for historical reasons, the values should not be modified. Consider using `char* const*` or ensure the string literal is not modified.
```suggestion
    const char* av[] = {argv[0], fexecve_test_flag, NULL};
    lseek(fd, 0, SEEK_SET);
    fexecve(fd, (char *const *)av, envp);
